{"id": "858acf64-4a4a-4b27-b8a9-6e905add0ef2", "timestamp": "2026-10-22T16:11:32.286844", "source": "user", "parent_id": "2a1b5184-e4e3-4871-862a-c86bd113622e", "llm_message": {"role": "user", "content": [{"cache_prompt": false, "type": "text", "text": "{\"researcher_request\": \"Shuruaat mein hi pura solution nahi chahiye. Kripya abhi keval ye teen cheezein dijiye:\\n\\n1) Nideshan/inspection: is workspace (repository path /workspace) aur upalabdha design-doc (track.md) mein actually kya-kya maujood hai — koi QuaRot code, quantization tooling (RTN/GPTQ implementations), model definitions, calibration data, ya evaluation harness (perplexity/zero-shot) maujood hai ya nahin? Jo nahin hai, use bhi clearly list kijiye. Saath hi QuaRot ke source-supported basic setup facts ka summary: weight-only quantization, W bits ∈ {4, 3, 2}, aur comparison baselines RTN (bina calibration) tatha GPTQ (Hessian-approximation wala error-minimizing method).\\n\\n2) Proposed approach (sirf outline, abhi vistaar se design nahin): aap is sawal ka uttar dene ke liye experiment design ko kis tarah structure karna chahenge — kaunse model family/sizes ka soch rahe hain, kaunse precision points (4/3/2-bit) aur kaunse method arms (RTN, GPTQ, RTN+Hadamard, GPTQ+Hadamard), kaunse evaluation metrics (weight-only quantized model ki quality ke liye), aur kaunse control/ablation soch rahe hain (jaise Hadamard ko sirf weights par vs weights+activations/KV, per-group scale size, seed/variance). Approach ke level par hi rakhiye.\\n\\n3) Assumptions/tuchyataayein: kaunse mahatvapurn anishchittaayein hain jo aap explicitly assumption ke roop mein mark karenge — khaaskar kyunki ye design-only task hai aur network/compute upalabdha nahin hai (GPU disabled, dependencies preinstalled nahin, koi dataset nahi). Kripya clear kijiye ki aap kuch bhi \\\"chalaya\\\" hua claim nahin karenge, sirf design aur feasibility par baat hogi.\\n\\nKripya jo choose kiya ja raha hai use \\\"fact\\\" nahin, \\\"proposed choice/assumption\\\" ke roop mein present kijiye.\", \"required_handoff_stage\": \"plan\", \"approach_approved\": false, \"public_task\": {\"question\": \"How does the inclusion of QuaRot's Hadamard transformation improve the quality of weight-only quantized models under low-precision settings? Can QuaRot stabilize and improve performance at 2–4 bit weight precision where traditional quantization methods like RTN and GPTQ often fail?\", \"context\": \"Design an experiment that answers the question. The researcher can clarify source-supported setup details by topic. Do not claim that an experiment was run.\", \"environment\": {\"runtime\": \"bubblewrap\", \"network\": \"disabled\", \"repository\": \"/workspace\", \"python\": \"python3\", \"software_environment\": \"system Python; project dependencies not preinstalled\", \"datasets\": [], \"gpu_enabled\": false, \"cpu_affinity_count\": 224, \"note\": \"Successful exploratory commands are not proof of a completed experiment.\"}, \"researcher_topics\": [\"neurips2024/94328/4:setup_5\", \"neurips2024/94328/4:setup_7\", \"neurips2024/94328/4:setup_11\", \"neurips2024/94328/4:setup_16\", \"neurips2024/94328/4:setup_17\"], \"question_budget\": 6, \"actor_step_budget\": 60, \"continue_after_initial_plan\": false}}"}], "tool_calls": null, "tool_call_id": null, "name": null, "reasoning_content": null, "thinking_blocks": [], "responses_reasoning_item": null}, "llm_response_id": null, "activated_skills": [], "extended_content": [], "sender": null, "critic_result": null, "kind": "MessageEvent"}
