s (GPTQ ~ 2–6 h for 7B on 1×A100 with 128×2048 calib; RTN ~ minutes); T(ppl) ~ 0.1–0.5 h per 7B; zero-shot 6 tasks ~ 1–3 h per 7B; per-block ΔPPL adds k forward-only passes.\nEstimate: primary grid 3 models × 25 runs ≈ 75 quant runs; dominant cost GPTQ runs = 3 bits × 3 methods? Actually GPTQ arms = 2 (GPTQ, GPTQ+Had) × 3 bits × 3 seeds for Had? Let's compute: GPTQ runs per model = 3 bits × (1 no-rot + 3 seeds rot) = 12; RTN runs = 3 × (1 + 3) = 12. GPTQ is the expensive one (Hessian accumulation + Cholesky). ~12 GPTQ runs × ~4 GPU-h (7B) ≈ 48 GPU-h per model; ×3 models ≈ 144 GPU-h; evals ~ 25 runs × 2 h × 3 = 150 GPU-h; ablations (7B only) ≈ 60 GPU-h; per-block curves ≈ 40 GPU-h → ≈ 400 GPU-h ≈ 1 week on 4×A100. 70B: ×~8 → 3000 GPU-h (2–3 weeks on 8×80GB) → recommend 70B only for top-line 4 arms × W2.\nStorage: 70B FP16 = 140 GB + quant checkpoints small; 7B = 13.5GB each. /workspace free 10.87 GB → cannot hold even one 7B FP16 checkpoint. So: cannot execute here.\nCan do here: Tier-0 (stdlib only, seconds), which I did.\nCannot: anything needing torch/transformers/datasets/network/GPU; deps install impossible (DNS blocked); /workspace 10.9 GB free; /tmp 1 TB but non-persistent across calls (observed); Python 3.14 → wheels for torch 2.1–2.3 (paper era) don't exist for 3.14 → environment rebuild needed.\nWhat a real run needs: 4–8× 80GB GPUs, ≥2 TB scratch, HF access to LLaMA-2/3 weights (gated) + C4/WikiText, torch/transformers/accelerate/lm-eval, 1–2 weeks wall clock.\n\n**G. Synthetic results labeling** — clearly separate: all numbers labelled \"ILLUSTRATIVE (synthetic)\" with the table.\n\nAlso mention: probe B v1 gave nonsense for GPTQ (bug: curvature approx + wrong scale indexing), showing why harness acceptance gates (E probe) must precede any real run — good honesty: iterate to correct implementation. Gates: round-trip error 4.4e-16, norm preservation 1.000000000000, MSE at 16/8/4 bits monotone decreasing, permutation-equivariance exact.\n\nAlso assumptions/