2192 1.004\\u20131.009. Dose-response: frac 0.001/0.01/0.05/0.2 \\u2192 0.283/0.071/0.129/0.611; magnitude 0/3/10/30/100 \\u2192 1.000/0.802/0.173/0.066/0.035.\\n- Controls N2/N3/N4 at 4/3/2 bits (ratio vs identity): permutation 1.00/1.00/1.00; sign-only 1.10/1.09/1.19; dense random orthogonal 0.34/0.25/0.27 vs randomized-Hadamard 0.18/0.13/0.16 \\u2192 Hadamard-specific, not \\\"any orthogonal transform\\\".\\n- Dose-response in layer count (mirror of A3): rotated-layer fraction 0/.25/.5/.75/1 \\u2192 1.000/0.706/0.495/0.297/0.159.\\n- Curvature-weighted objective (GPTQ's own loss), 4-arm toy linear layer with activation-outlier channels, 2 bits: RTN 0.550, GPTQ 0.733, RTN+Had 0.126, GPTQ+Had 0.277 (at 4 bits: 0.0186 / 0.0256 / 0.0023 / 0.0074) \\u2192 motivates the redundancy hypothesis M4/F1; curvature diagonal max/mean 34.5 \\u2192 1.19 after Hadamard. Note the first toy-GPTQ version was buggy (0.49 vs 0.019) and had to be fixed to a proper Cholesky-based update \\u2014 direct evidence for the harness-gate requirement C1.\\n- Harness gates implemented and passing: rotation round-trip error 4.44e-16; norm preservation 1.000000000000; quantizer MSE monotone in bits (9.5e-9 / 6.0e-4 / 1.8e-1 at 16/8/4b); group-quant MSE exactly permutation-equivariant (311.5729 before and after permutation).\\n- Corrected-basis check (A1 probe): measuring error in the ORIGINAL basis after un-rotation reproduces the same ~0.08\\u20130.12 ratios, confirming Frobenius invariance means M1 is comparable across arms.\\n- Iteration count: 5 probe revisions (dim power-of-2 requirement for FWHM, per-row scales, proper Cholesky factor) \\u2014 all inside the sandbox, all documented above.\", \"assumptions\": [\"FIXED by the task: weight-only quantization (activations FP), W bits {4,3,2}, and RTN/GPTQ as the two baselines. Everything else in the design is a proposed choice.\", \"Frozen primary config C* (asymmetric per-group, g*=128, exclude embed/lm_head/norms/rotary) is my proposed pre-registration to prevent the sign-flip my probes exposed; its agreement with the paper's actual weight-only recipe is an assumption pending confirmation.\", \"The QuaRot setup facts I recited (offline folding, randomized Hadamard, group-128 weight-only recipe, reported W2 degradation of GPTQ/RTN) come from prior knowledge of the paper, NOT from any file in this workspace.\", \"Model set (LLaMA-2 7B/13B, LLaMA-3 8B, TinyLlama smoke, optional 70B), 3 seeds for Had arms, thresholds (x3 stability, x5 fail, x10 collapse, B(2)>=2*B(4)) are proposed pre-registered choices, not task requirements.\", \"Design-only: no experiment was run; no perplexity, accuracy or magnitude statement about any real model is made or implied. All numeric values in the design are labeled [SYN] synthetic and exist only to validate code/metric behaviour and hypothesis direction.\", \"A real execution is assumed to occur on another machine (GPUs, persistent storage, model weights, calibration corpora, 3.10/3.11 Python environment); this workspace cannot host it.\"], \"uncertainties\": [\"Quantizer configuration can reverse the direction of the Hadamard effect (measured: 3.3x worse under symmetric 2-bit vs 12x better under asymmetric). Freezing C* removes this ambiguity for the primary claim but means the primary claim is config-conditional by construction.\", \"Redundancy vs complementarity of Hadamard and GPTQ is genuinely unknown for real LLM weights; my toy suggested RTN+Hadamard beat GPTQ+Hadamard, but toy curvature is not transformer curvature, so the interaction term's sign is an open empirical question this design measures rather than assumes.\", \"Group-size fade-out: whether Hadamard's advantage survives at g=32/64 on real weights is untested; if it fades, the paper-level headline becomes 'rotation substitutes for fine-grained scaling', a different claim.\", \"Hadamard-specificity: the dense-orthogonal control on synthetic data landed between identity and Hadamard, so a real 'flat-spectrum matters' claim needs that control run on real weight matrices; the 1/n Hadamard blocks for non-power-of-2 or head-dimension mismatch also need a concrete implementation choice (per-head Hadamard) not fixed here.\", \"Whether the reported weight-only benefit depends on residual/activation-side rotations cannot be fully excluded by any weight-only arm; the C2 control bounds but does not eliminate it.\", \"External feasibility only: my GPU-hour estimates are order-of-magnitude planning numbers derived from arm counts and model sizes, not from any measurement in this environment.\", \"Setup details listed in section I (g*, grid conventions, excluded tensors, GPTQ calibration corpus, PPL windowing, zero-shot list) remain unconfirmed because no source document or code exists in the workspace.\"], \"stage\": \"result\"}", "kind": "ActionEvent"}
